'''''Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide''''' is a [[canon]] reference book for the film ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''. Written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]], it was released by [[Dorling Kindersley]] on [[December 16]], [[2016]], the same day as the film.

==Publisher's summary==
''The essential, comprehensive guide to ''Rogue One: A Star Wars Story™''.''

''This exciting reference format accompanies the eagerly anticipated, first-ever standalone ''Star Wars™ ''movie: ''Rogue One''. This beautifully detailed title features in-depth character profiles, plus 5 newly commissioned and fully annotated cross-sections of vehicles and mapped-out locations. With clear and authoritative text, this book is packed with essential information-and presented alongside stunning stills from the movie.''<ref name="DK" />

===Back cover===
''THE ULTIMATE GUIDE TO ''ROGUE ONE: A STAR WARS STORY

''Produced in collaboration with Lucasfilm and written by renowned ''Star Wars'' expert Pablo Hidalgo, ''Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide'' combines lavish movie stills with in-depth character profiles, fascinating insider information, and incredible cross-sections.''

''See inside the rebels{{'s}} U-wing gunship • Explore new planets and ancient worlds • Discover the origins of the death troopers • Learn about kyber crystals and Death Star technology • And more!''

''STEP INSIDE AND JOIN A REBELLION BUILT ON HOPE.''

==Continuity==
*[[Garven Dreis]]'s last name is misspelled "Dries" (p. 46).
*[[Darkknell]] is misspelled as "Darknell" (p. 53).
*[[Coastal defender stormtrooper|Shoretroopers]] are mistakenly called [[Desert stormtrooper|sandtroopers]] (p. 153).
*General [[Antoc Merrick|Merrick]] is mistakenly referred to as Draven (p. 170).

